 - Writes require the `contributor` or `manager` role in the project. Users who can read but not write get 403.
 - Contributors may only modify tasks assigned to themselves, and may not reassign tasks. Managers may modify any task.
 - Only managers may delete tasks.
+- Moving a task needs the same rights as editing it in the source project
+  (managers any task, contributors only their own). The actor must also be a
+  contributor or manager of the destination, which must be readable (else 404)
+  and not archived (else 409). Moving to the task's current project → 400. The
+  task keeps its assignee, so the assignee must be a contributor or manager of
+  the destination → else 400.
 - Archived projects reject all writes with 409 (reads still work).
 - A task ID that does not belong to the project in the path → 404.
 
